  m_text: "From 1990 to 2010, Northeast China\u2019s morning markets mainly served
    local residents as everyday community spaces. Vendors were mostly nearby residents
    and small business owners, selling daily necessities and traditional snacks.
    Unlike today\u2019s internet-famous morning markets, which focus more on tourism
    and city branding, early morning markets of this period were more closely connected
    to local life and neighborhood relationships."
