  m_text: Before formal morning markets were established in Harbin, breakfast vendors
    mainly gathered near factories and residential areas. After the reform and opening-up
    period, small private businesses began to emerge, with vendors selling foods
    such as steamed buns and fried dough sticks to serve workers and local residents.
    These mobile stalls became the early form of later morning markets and reflected
    changes in urban lifestyles.
